1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,150
In the beginning, there was only the blank page.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:10,750
Then someone wrote the first word.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,950
Fire.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,150
Water.

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,350
Wind.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:26,750
In the land of Hinomoto, words have power.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:33,950
Those who write with spirit ink are called Fudeshi... Brush Masters.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,550
But twelve years ago, something came from beyond the margins of the world.

9
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:48,950
The Blank. A hunger that erases everything it touches. Names. Homes. Memories.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,450
One master stood against it... and with a single word, sealed it away.

11
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:01,950
Then he vanished, and left behind only that word.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,950
Now... that word is beginning to fade.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,322
[Kakeru] HEY, WORLD! ARE YOU LISTENING?!

14
00:01:13,372 --> 00:01:16,146
[Kakeru] My name is Kakeru Sumizome!

15
00:01:16,196 --> 00:01:20,458
[Kakeru] My handwriting is the worst in the whole village...

16
00:01:20,508 --> 00:01:22,058
[Nijimi] Niji! Niji!

17
00:01:22,108 --> 00:01:25,564
[Kakeru] Hey! You didn't have to agree so fast!

18
00:01:25,614 --> 00:01:29,566
[Kakeru] But someday... everybody's gonna read my name!

19
00:01:29,616 --> 00:01:33,166
[Kakeru] I'M GONNA BE THE GREATEST BRUSH MASTER IN HISTORY!

20
00:03:17,616 --> 00:03:22,436
[Kakeru] Zzz... one more stroke... and it looks just like a dragon...

21
00:03:24,086 --> 00:03:25,868
[Nijimi] Niji! Niji!

22
00:03:25,918 --> 00:03:28,754
[Kakeru] Five more minutes, Nijimi...

23
00:03:28,804 --> 00:03:30,454
[Nijimi] NIJIIIIII!!

24
00:03:30,504 --> 00:03:34,054
[Kakeru] Okay, okay! I'm up! What's the big deal? It's just a normal day...

25
00:03:36,304 --> 00:03:38,054
[Kakeru] ...EXAM DAY?!

26
00:03:39,204 --> 00:03:42,754
[Kakeru] Morning, Grandma! Today's the day. Watch me, okay?

27
00:03:43,304 --> 00:03:44,754
[Nijimi] Niji.

28
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:53,246
[Granny Ume] Kakeru-chan! Good luck at the exam today!

29
00:03:53,296 --> 00:03:57,496
[Kakeru] Thanks, Granny Ume! I'll come back a real Fudeshi!

30
00:03:57,546 --> 00:04:01,374
[Tea Shop Owner] And don't you DARE write my shop sign again!

31
00:04:01,424 --> 00:04:05,686
[Tea Shop Owner] Three years! It STILL says 'fish' instead of 'tea'!

32
00:04:05,736 --> 00:04:08,882
[Kakeru] It's not wrong! It's... artistic!

33
00:04:08,932 --> 00:04:11,520
[Nijimi] Niji... (No. It is not.)

34
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:14,320
[Little Girl] Ah! My kite! Come back!

35
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:19,002
[Kakeru] Don't cry! I'll get it back for you!

36
00:04:19,052 --> 00:04:22,136
[Nijimi] Niji?! (With YOUR handwriting?!)

37
00:04:22,186 --> 00:04:24,650
[Kakeru] Wind! Nine strokes! 風!

38
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,536
[Little Girl] Wow! Thank you, big brother!

39
00:04:34,586 --> 00:04:38,662
[Little Girl] Your writing looks really funny... but it works!

40
00:04:38,712 --> 00:04:41,796
[Kakeru] Funny-looking... but it works...

41
00:04:41,846 --> 00:04:44,062
[Kakeru] Heh. I'll take it!

42
00:04:46,512 --> 00:04:49,906
[Kanemaru] Well, well. If it isn't Scribble-boy.

43
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,234
[Lackey] Hehe! Scribble-boy!

44
00:04:52,284 --> 00:04:57,910
[Kanemaru] Still planning to take the exam with handwriting like chicken footprints?

45
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:01,354
[Kakeru] Hey! Chickens have GREAT handwriting!

46
00:05:02,304 --> 00:05:05,202
[Kakeru] ...Wait. That came out wrong.

47
00:05:05,252 --> 00:05:09,266
[Kanemaru] My father paid for the new exam hall, you know.

48
00:05:09,316 --> 00:05:13,268
[Kanemaru] They'll pass me before I even pick up a brush.

49
00:05:13,318 --> 00:05:18,138
[Kakeru] Then I'll pass with my own hand! No money, no help. Just me!

50
00:05:18,188 --> 00:05:22,574
[Kanemaru] Hah! See you at the bottom of the list, Scribble-boy.

51
00:05:25,224 --> 00:05:27,378
[Nijimi] Niji! Niji! Niji!

52
00:05:27,428 --> 00:05:30,388
[Kakeru] The bell! The exam's starting!

53
00:05:30,438 --> 00:05:33,522
[Kakeru] I'm NOT missing this! Ink it in!

54
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:41,636
[Gonda] LISTEN UP, CANDIDATES!

55
00:05:41,686 --> 00:05:44,832
[Gonda] I am Gonda Tetsuzo, your proctor!

56
00:05:44,882 --> 00:05:49,578
[Gonda] The test is simple. You will write ONE word in spirit ink.

57
00:05:49,628 --> 00:05:52,898
[Gonda] If your word comes alive, you pass.

58
00:05:54,348 --> 00:05:56,698
[Gonda] THIS is a living word.

59
00:05:56,748 --> 00:06:01,196
[Gonda] If it just lies there on the paper like a dead fish...

60
00:06:01,246 --> 00:06:05,942
[Gonda] ...you go home and sell noodles for the rest of your life!

61
00:06:08,892 --> 00:06:12,782
[Kakeru] I'M HERE! Kakeru Sumizome, present and ready!

62
00:06:12,832 --> 00:06:15,296
[Gonda] You're LATE, Sumizome!

63
00:06:15,346 --> 00:06:19,608
[Kakeru] Technically, I'm really early for next year's exam!

64
00:06:19,658 --> 00:06:21,812
[Gonda] And what is THAT?

65
00:06:22,762 --> 00:06:26,714
[Kakeru] Uh... th-that's my... very ink-colored... cat?

66
00:06:26,764 --> 00:06:28,514
[Nijimi] ...Meow.

67
00:06:28,564 --> 00:06:29,914
[Gonda] ...

68
00:06:29,964 --> 00:06:31,932
[Gonda] GET. IN. LINE.

69
00:06:32,982 --> 00:06:37,926
[Kakeru] Hey! You're Shiori Kaisho, right? From the famous Kaisho clan?

70
00:06:39,476 --> 00:06:42,684
[Kakeru] I'm Kakeru! Let's both pass, okay?

71
00:06:42,734 --> 00:06:45,198
[Shiori] Your scarf is crooked.

72
00:06:45,248 --> 00:06:47,774
[Shiori] Your brush is unwashed.

73
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:50,970
[Shiori] And you are standing on my paper.

74
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:52,770
[Kakeru] WHOA! Sorry, sorry!

75
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:55,780
[Gonda] First candidate! Number seven!

76
00:07:00,430 --> 00:07:02,708
[Gonda] ...Dead fish. FAIL!

77
00:07:04,558 --> 00:07:08,634
[Kakeru] Whoa... he's actually serious about the noodles.

78
00:07:08,684 --> 00:07:11,024
[Gonda] Next! Kanemaru Toru!

79
00:07:11,074 --> 00:07:13,662
[Kanemaru] Watch closely, peasants.

80
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:20,776
[Gonda] ...Weak. Barely alive.

81
00:07:20,826 --> 00:07:22,918
[Gonda] But alive. PASS.

82
00:07:22,968 --> 00:07:24,718
[Kanemaru] Naturally.

83
00:07:24,768 --> 00:07:27,728
[Gonda] Next! Candidate number twelve!

84
00:07:32,078 --> 00:07:35,224
[Gonda] ...Pass. Somebody get me a towel.

85
00:07:35,274 --> 00:07:37,614
[Gonda] Next! Kaisho Shiori!

86
00:07:37,664 --> 00:07:39,814
[Spectator] That's the Kaisho heiress!

87
00:07:39,864 --> 00:07:43,214
[Spectator] They say she wrote her first living word when she was four years old!

88
00:07:43,864 --> 00:07:46,814
[Shiori] Precision. Balance. Promise.

89
00:07:58,064 --> 00:08:00,094
[Kakeru] WHOA! SO COOL!!

90
00:08:00,144 --> 00:08:03,600
[Gonda] Perfect stroke order. Perfect balance.

91
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,866
[Gonda] PASS. With honors.

92
00:08:07,816 --> 00:08:10,900
[Gonda] Last candidate! Sumizome Kakeru!

93
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:15,522
[Kanemaru] Oh, this should be good. Here comes the chicken scratch.

94
00:08:15,572 --> 00:08:17,122
[Nijimi] Niji! Niji!

95
00:08:17,172 --> 00:08:22,178
[Kakeru] Okay. Fire. Four strokes. I've practiced this a thousand times.

96
00:08:22,228 --> 00:08:24,134
[Kakeru] Ink it in...!

97
00:08:35,384 --> 00:08:38,334
[Kanemaru] A FROG! He wrote 'fire' and got a FROG!

98
00:08:38,384 --> 00:08:41,840
[Kakeru] It's a FIRE frog! That counts, right?!

99
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:44,230
[Gonda] Stroke order: wrong.

100
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:46,248
[Gonda] Balance: none.

101
00:08:46,298 --> 00:08:48,514
[Gonda] Shape: unreadable.

102
00:08:48,564 --> 00:08:50,714
[Gonda] FAIL.

103
00:08:52,564 --> 00:08:56,144
[Gonda] Come back next year, Sumizome. Or don't.

104
00:08:58,194 --> 00:09:01,154
[Shiori] Words are a promise, Sumizome.

105
00:09:01,204 --> 00:09:05,900
[Shiori] If you can't keep the shape... you can't keep the promise.

106
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:08,972
[Kakeru] ...Then I'll make my own shape!

107
00:09:10,122 --> 00:09:13,578
[Shiori] A shape no one can read is just noise.

108
00:09:21,228 --> 00:09:22,978
[Gonda] ...Strange.

109
00:09:23,028 --> 00:09:27,042
[Gonda] Hours have passed. That ink still hasn't dried.

110
00:09:33,492 --> 00:09:37,196
[Kakeru] Four strokes, Nijimi. Just four strokes...

111
00:09:37,246 --> 00:09:40,206
[Kakeru] ...and I still couldn't do it.

112
00:09:40,256 --> 00:09:42,006
[Nijimi] Niji...

113
00:09:42,056 --> 00:09:45,202
[Kakeru] Everybody laughed. Even Shiori...

114
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:51,064
[Kakeru] Well, she didn't laugh. She just looked at me like I was a spelling mistake.

115
00:09:51,114 --> 00:09:56,802
[Kakeru] Hey. You remember? You're the only word I ever wrote that actually worked.

116
00:10:00,252 --> 00:10:04,266
[Little Kakeru] The other kids say my writing looks like worms!

117
00:10:04,316 --> 00:10:06,718
[Grandma Chiyo] Hmm? Let Grandma see.

118
00:10:06,768 --> 00:10:10,224
[Grandma Chiyo] Oh my. These are very energetic worms.

119
00:10:10,274 --> 00:10:12,024
[Little Kakeru] Grandma!

120
00:10:12,074 --> 00:10:14,476
[Grandma Chiyo] Kakeru. Listen to me.

121
00:10:14,526 --> 00:10:18,044
[Grandma Chiyo] A word is a wish you send to the world.

122
00:10:18,094 --> 00:10:22,790
[Grandma Chiyo] Neat or messy... the world hears it, if you truly mean it.

123
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:25,676
[Little Kakeru] ...Then I wish for a friend.

124
00:10:25,726 --> 00:10:28,810
[Little Kakeru] A friend who never, ever leaves.

125
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:33,210
[Nijimi] Niji!

126
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,610
[Little Kakeru] Whoa!

127
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:38,358
[Grandma Chiyo] See? The world was listening.

128
00:10:38,408 --> 00:10:42,484
[Kakeru] Grandma said the world hears it, if you mean it.

129
00:10:42,534 --> 00:10:45,680
[Kakeru] I meant it today. I really did...

130
00:10:45,730 --> 00:10:49,280
[Bokusai] Then maybe the world was a little hard of hearing today.

131
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:56,840
[Kakeru] Wh-who are you?! How long have you been sitting there?!

132
00:10:56,890 --> 00:11:00,036
[Bokusai] Since before you started sulking.

133
00:11:00,086 --> 00:11:04,224
[Bokusai] The fish don't bite when you sigh that loud. Hic!

134
00:11:04,274 --> 00:11:08,908
[Bokusai] That frog at the exam today... that was yours, wasn't it?

135
00:11:08,958 --> 00:11:12,538
[Kakeru] You saw that? Great. Go ahead and laugh.

136
00:11:12,588 --> 00:11:14,494
[Bokusai] Laugh? Kid...

137
00:11:14,544 --> 00:11:17,380
[Bokusai] ...your frog is still alive.

138
00:11:20,030 --> 00:11:22,494
[Kakeru] It's... still burning?

139
00:11:22,544 --> 00:11:28,728
[Bokusai] Living words fade after a few minutes. Even the Kaisho girl's dragon is long gone.

140
00:11:28,778 --> 00:11:32,172
[Bokusai] But yours is still here. Hours later.

141
00:11:32,222 --> 00:11:36,732
[Bokusai] Tell me, kid. Why do you want to be a Fudeshi so badly?

142
00:11:36,782 --> 00:11:39,246
[Kakeru] ...My grandma was one.

143
00:11:39,296 --> 00:11:45,790
[Kakeru] Just a small-town Fudeshi. She wrote 'heal' for sick kids, and 'warm' for cold winters.

144
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:49,854
[Kakeru] Nobody outside this village ever knew her name.

145
00:11:49,904 --> 00:11:54,414
[Kakeru] But if I become the greatest Brush Master in history...

146
00:11:54,464 --> 00:12:01,826
[Kakeru] ...then everyone will know about the village Fudeshi who believed in a kid with terrible handwriting.

147
00:12:03,276 --> 00:12:06,856
[Bokusai] ...Hm. That's a better reason than most.

148
00:12:06,906 --> 00:12:11,664
[Bokusai] I've seen strokes like yours before. A long, long time ago.

149
00:12:11,714 --> 00:12:14,488
[Kakeru] Huh? Where? Who wrote them?

150
00:12:14,538 --> 00:12:18,288
[Bokusai] Go home, Scribbles. Tonight is going to be loud.

151
00:12:18,338 --> 00:12:20,926
[Kakeru] Hey, wait! Who ARE you?!

152
00:12:20,976 --> 00:12:24,618
[Bokusai] Just an old drunk who likes fishing. Hic!

153
00:12:28,468 --> 00:12:31,218
[Kakeru] ...Still burning, huh?

154
00:12:49,668 --> 00:12:52,818
[Lord Kaisho (letter)] Shiori. A Kaisho does not make mistakes.

155
00:12:52,868 --> 00:12:57,018
[Lord Kaisho (letter)] Pass with honors. Anything less, and do not bother coming home.

156
00:12:57,068 --> 00:13:00,090
[Shiori] I passed with honors, Father...

157
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:03,224
[Shiori] So why does it feel like I lost?

158
00:13:04,474 --> 00:13:08,860
[Shiori] That idiot's frog... it was still moving when I left.

159
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:13,048
[Shiori] Living words don't last that long. Not even mine.

160
00:13:13,098 --> 00:13:15,252
[Shiori] ...One more time.

161
00:13:17,902 --> 00:13:19,746
[Gate Guard] Quiet night.

162
00:13:19,796 --> 00:13:23,686
[Gate Guard] Too quiet. Even the crickets stopped singing.

163
00:13:26,536 --> 00:13:29,806
[Gate Guard] Who goes there?! Identify yourself!

164
00:13:29,856 --> 00:13:31,806
[Nashi] Identify...?

165
00:13:31,856 --> 00:13:36,366
[Nashi] I have no name to give you. Hakushi erased it long ago.

166
00:13:39,416 --> 00:13:41,942
[Gate Guard] M-my word... it's gone!

167
00:13:41,992 --> 00:13:45,448
[Nashi] Words are only stains on a clean page.

168
00:13:53,898 --> 00:13:56,300
[Nijimi] Niji... niji niji...!

169
00:13:56,350 --> 00:13:59,124
[Kakeru] Mm... Nijimi? What's wrong?

170
00:14:00,974 --> 00:14:04,740
[Kakeru] That light... it's coming from the academy!

171
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:13,168
[Kanemaru] S-Scribble-boy?! Don't go that way! A monster is erasing the academy!

172
00:14:13,218 --> 00:14:16,798
[Kakeru] The academy?! Is anyone still in there?!

173
00:14:16,848 --> 00:14:21,978
[Kanemaru] The Kaisho girl was training late... b-but that's not my problem!

174
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:26,352
[Kanemaru] I'm going to get help! Definitely getting help! Bye!

175
00:14:26,402 --> 00:14:28,152
[Kakeru] Shiori...!

176
00:14:31,202 --> 00:14:33,852
[Gonda] Hakushi?! In MY academy?!

177
00:14:33,902 --> 00:14:39,094
[Nashi] Instructor Gonda. You fail children for messy strokes, do you not?

178
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:42,724
[Nashi] Then we are not so different, you and I.

179
00:14:42,774 --> 00:14:45,486
[Gonda] Don't you DARE compare us!

180
00:14:50,536 --> 00:14:55,728
[Nashi] Your words are loud, Instructor. But loud is not the same as true.

181
00:14:57,978 --> 00:15:00,528
[Gonda] Ngh... somebody... run...

182
00:15:03,378 --> 00:15:05,532
[Shiori] Stop right there.

183
00:15:05,582 --> 00:15:09,534
[Shiori] This is Hitsuzan Academy. You are trespassing.

184
00:15:09,584 --> 00:15:14,094
[Nashi] Ah. The Kaisho girl. The one with the beautiful dragon.

185
00:15:14,144 --> 00:15:19,770
[Shiori] White coat. Porcelain mask. You're from Hakushi... the cult of the Blank.

186
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,842
[Nashi] A cult? No, no. We are editors.

187
00:15:22,892 --> 00:15:27,960
[Nashi] The world is so crowded with words. We are simply... tidying up.

188
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,908
[Shiori] Then allow me to correct you.

189
00:15:34,458 --> 00:15:36,798
[Nashi] Lovely stroke order.

190
00:15:39,448 --> 00:15:41,850
[Shiori] Then how about THIS?!

191
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:48,042
[Nashi] Ah. You are getting faster. How diligent.

192
00:15:48,092 --> 00:15:50,370
[Shiori] Why won't it land?!

193
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:54,372
[Nashi] Because your words are perfect, Kaisho Shiori.

194
00:15:54,422 --> 00:15:59,118
[Nashi] Every line exactly where the dictionary says it should be.

195
00:15:59,168 --> 00:16:02,128
[Nashi] Neat words are easy to read...

196
00:16:03,078 --> 00:16:05,428
[Nashi] ...and easy to erase.

197
00:16:09,978 --> 00:16:11,946
[Shiori] My... brush...

198
00:16:11,996 --> 00:16:15,746
[Nashi] Don't worry. Soon you won't even remember you had one.

199
00:16:15,796 --> 00:16:18,756
[Shiori] Mother... Father... I'm sorry.

200
00:16:18,806 --> 00:16:21,642
[Shiori] I couldn't keep the shape...

201
00:16:21,692 --> 00:16:23,242
[Kakeru] HEY, CHALK-FACE!

202
00:16:25,492 --> 00:16:27,642
[Kakeru] Get away from her!

203
00:16:27,692 --> 00:16:32,202
[Shiori] Sumizome?! You idiot, run! You can't even write 'fire'!

204
00:16:32,252 --> 00:16:34,158
[Kakeru] Yeah. I know.

205
00:16:34,208 --> 00:16:38,656
[Kakeru] But I'm not gonna stand here and watch you get erased!

206
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:42,782
[Nashi] Ah... the boy with the frog. The one who failed.

207
00:16:42,832 --> 00:16:46,412
[Kakeru] I failed the exam. I'm NOT failing this!

208
00:16:48,962 --> 00:16:52,976
[Nashi] Messy words are still words. And all words end.

209
00:16:56,526 --> 00:16:58,742
[Shiori] Stop it! Just run!

210
00:16:58,792 --> 00:17:00,342
[Kakeru] Nope!

211
00:17:00,392 --> 00:17:04,964
[Kakeru] Grandma said a Fudeshi's brush exists to protect people.

212
00:17:05,014 --> 00:17:09,524
[Kakeru] If I run away now... I'll never get to call myself one.

213
00:17:09,574 --> 00:17:13,154
[Nashi] Why do you keep writing? You cannot win.

214
00:17:13,204 --> 00:17:17,094
[Kakeru] Because... my grandma told me something once.

215
00:17:17,144 --> 00:17:20,662
[Grandma Chiyo] A word is a wish you send to the world.

216
00:17:20,712 --> 00:17:23,052
[Kakeru] A word... is a wish.

217
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:27,252
[Nijimi] Niji...

218
00:17:27,302 --> 00:17:31,316
[Kakeru] Nijimi... you were my wish. My very first word.

219
00:17:31,366 --> 00:17:34,574
[Kakeru] And you never left. Not even once.

220
00:17:34,624 --> 00:17:38,762
[Kakeru] So this time... I'm gonna wish for something BIG.

221
00:17:42,412 --> 00:17:47,108
[Kakeru] You said neat words are easy to read... and easy to erase?

222
00:17:48,158 --> 00:17:51,508
[Kakeru] Then I'll write something NOBODY can read!

223
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:59,676
[Nashi] It won't erase...? Why won't it ERASE?!

224
00:17:59,726 --> 00:18:03,740
[Nashi] What is this word?! It's not in any dictionary!

225
00:18:03,790 --> 00:18:06,626
[Kakeru] I don't know what it says...

226
00:18:06,676 --> 00:18:09,026
[Kakeru] ...but I MEAN IT!

227
00:18:09,076 --> 00:18:12,626
[Kakeru] Doodle Style... ROARING SCRIBBLE!!!

228
00:18:19,076 --> 00:18:22,036
[Nashi] Kami-moji... The First Script.

229
00:18:22,086 --> 00:18:26,038
[Nashi] So it wasn't sealed away with him after all...

230
00:18:26,088 --> 00:18:30,660
[Nashi] Sumizome Kakeru. The Master will want to know about you.

231
00:18:34,110 --> 00:18:38,000
[Kakeru] Heh... Did you see that, Nijimi? It worked...

232
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:41,072
[Shiori] ...What did you write just now?

233
00:18:41,122 --> 00:18:42,872
[Kakeru] No idea.

234
00:18:44,522 --> 00:18:46,672
[Shiori] ...Idiot.

235
00:18:46,722 --> 00:18:50,072
[Gonda] That stroke... it is still burning...

236
00:18:50,122 --> 00:18:52,338
[Shiori] Sumizome wrote it.

237
00:18:52,388 --> 00:18:54,956
[Gonda] ...Impossible.

238
00:18:59,006 --> 00:19:01,656
[Kakeru] Mm... huh? Where am I...?

239
00:19:01,706 --> 00:19:03,922
[Kakeru] AH! The old drunk!

240
00:19:03,972 --> 00:19:08,668
[Bokusai] Morning, Scribbles. You slept like a log. A very loud log.

241
00:19:08,718 --> 00:19:13,414
[Bokusai] That stroke you wrote last night. Do you know what it was?

242
00:19:13,464 --> 00:19:16,238
[Kakeru] Uh... a really cool doodle?

243
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:19,124
[Bokusai] Kami-moji. The First Script.

244
00:19:19,174 --> 00:19:24,862
[Bokusai] Words that existed before dictionaries. Before rules. Before stroke order.

245
00:19:24,912 --> 00:19:28,554
[Bokusai] Only one man in history could write it...

246
00:19:28,604 --> 00:19:32,990
[Bokusai] ...the master who sealed the Blank, twelve years ago.

247
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:35,628
[Kakeru] The legendary master...?

248
00:19:35,678 --> 00:19:40,002
[Kakeru] Wait. How do YOU know all this? Who are you, really?

249
00:19:41,252 --> 00:19:46,072
[Bokusai] Me? I'm just the old man who taught him how to hold a brush.

250
00:19:46,122 --> 00:19:47,872
[Kakeru] EHHHHH?!

251
00:19:47,922 --> 00:19:52,804
[Bokusai] Hakushi will come for you now. They erase whatever they fear.

252
00:19:52,854 --> 00:19:56,434
[Bokusai] So. Do you want to keep failing exams...

253
00:19:56,484 --> 00:20:00,064
[Bokusai] ...or do you want to learn how to write?

254
00:20:00,114 --> 00:20:03,260
[Kakeru] Write properly? You mean... neat?

255
00:20:03,310 --> 00:20:06,022
[Bokusai] Neat? Ha! No. I mean LOUD.

256
00:20:06,072 --> 00:20:07,822
[Kakeru] Loud...?

257
00:20:07,872 --> 00:20:09,422
[Bokusai] Watch.

258
00:20:14,172 --> 00:20:17,380
[Kakeru] WHOA! He split the CLOUDS in half!

259
00:20:17,430 --> 00:20:22,126
[Bokusai] One stroke. One meaning. Meant with everything you've got.

260
00:20:22,176 --> 00:20:25,012
[Bokusai] That's all writing ever was.

261
00:20:25,062 --> 00:20:30,564
[Kakeru] Then teach me! I'll be the greatest Brush Master in history! Ink it in!

262
00:20:30,614 --> 00:20:33,946
[Bokusai] Hmph. First lesson: wash your brush.

263
00:20:33,996 --> 00:20:35,446
[Kakeru] EH?!

264
00:20:35,496 --> 00:20:37,446
[Nijimi] Niji! Niji! Niji!

265
00:20:39,896 --> 00:20:41,446
[Shiori] Sumizome.

266
00:20:41,496 --> 00:20:44,766
[Kakeru] Shiori! Are you okay? Your brush...

267
00:20:44,816 --> 00:20:47,714
[Shiori] ...Thank you. For last night.

268
00:20:47,764 --> 00:20:52,212
[Shiori] But don't misunderstand. This doesn't make us friends.

269
00:20:52,262 --> 00:20:56,214
[Kakeru] So we're rivals? Cool! Rivals are even better!

270
00:20:56,264 --> 00:20:57,614
[Shiori] Hmph.

271
00:21:01,064 --> 00:21:03,962
[Shiori] Kami-moji... Sumizome Kakeru.

272
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:08,088
[Shiori] Next time, I'll be the one doing the protecting.

273
00:21:11,738 --> 00:21:16,868
[Nashi] Forgive me, my King. The seal-breaker's script... a boy wrote it.

274
00:21:16,918 --> 00:21:20,002
[The White King] The First Script has awakened...

275
00:21:20,052 --> 00:21:25,058
[Nashi] His stroke would not erase, my King. It burned through my mask.

276
00:21:25,108 --> 00:21:29,990
[The White King] Of course. The First Script cannot be erased. Only forgotten.

277
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:32,070
[The White King] How delightful.

278
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:36,252
[The White King] Find the boy. And bring me his name.

279
00:23:09,302 --> 00:23:13,874
[Kakeru] Kakeru here! Old man Bokusai's training is totally nuts!

280
00:23:13,924 --> 00:23:17,194
[Kakeru] He wants me to write with my FEET?!

281
00:23:17,244 --> 00:23:20,080
[Kakeru] And Shiori wants a rematch?!

282
00:23:20,130 --> 00:23:26,580
[Kakeru] Next time on Kotodama: The Brush That Doesn't Write! Ink it in!
